---
import '../../styles/ports.css'

import { ButtonLink, Eyebrow, Icon, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import { previewHref, wallpaperDesigns, wallpaperHref } from '../../../../../artwork/wallpaper-catalog.mjs'
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro'
---
<ProductLayout name="Wallpaper appearance" slug="gallery/appearance" pageKind="guide" title="Light and dark wallpapers for Mac and iPhone — Santi020k" description="Download paired macOS HEIC wallpapers and learn how to switch saved iPhone wallpaper pairs with Shortcuts or Focus.">
  <section class="site-shell port-hero">
    <div><Eyebrow>For the rhythm of your day</Eyebrow><h1>A different light. The same feeling.</h1><p class="lede">Keep the wallpaper you love as your screen moves between light and dark. One paired file for Mac. Two saved setups and a simple automation for iPhone.</p><div class="port-actions"><ButtonLink variant="unstyled" class="port-button port-button-primary" href="#downloads">Choose a Mac wallpaper</ButtonLink><ButtonLink variant="unstyled" class="port-button port-button-secondary" href="#iphone">Set up iPhone switching</ButtonLink></div></div>
    <figure class="port-figure appearance-pair"><img src={previewHref('halo', 'light')} alt="Halo in pale lilac for light appearance" width="1920" height="1080" /><img src={previewHref('halo', 'dark')} alt="Halo in deep violet for dark appearance" width="1920" height="1080" /><figcaption>Halo · Two appearances, paired in one Mac wallpaper.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section id="install" class="site-shell port-section"><Eyebrow>On your Mac</Eyebrow><h2>Let the wallpaper follow your appearance.</h2><div class="port-columns"><ol class="port-steps"><li><h3>Save a paired HEIC</h3><p>Choose a design below and keep its file in a permanent folder. Each HEIC contains the original desktop composition in light and dark.</p></li><li><h3>Add it in Wallpaper settings</h3><p>Open System Settings → Wallpaper, choose Add Photo or Choose File, and select the HEIC. Where offered, choose Automatic in the wallpaper’s appearance menu.</p></li><li><h3>Choose your system appearance</h3><p>In System Settings → Appearance, select Light, Dark, or Auto. Auto follows your Mac’s day and night schedule. Labels and custom-wallpaper controls vary by macOS version.</p></li></ol><aside class="port-card"><h3>Two still images, paired</h3><p>These files switch between two appearances. They do not animate, track the sun, or provide a video screen saver.</p><p>If your macOS version imports the file as a still image, use the separate light and dark images from the gallery. Keep your previous wallpaper available until the pair works on your Mac.</p><Link href="https://support.apple.com/guide/mac-help/mchlp1103/mac" newTab>Apple’s Wallpaper settings guide</Link></aside></div></section>
  <section id="downloads" class="site-shell port-section" aria-labelledby="pairing-heading">
    <div class="appearance-heading">
      <div><Eyebrow>One design. Two appearances.</Eyebrow><h2 id="pairing-heading">Find your <span>day-to-night</span> pairing.</h2></div>
      <div class="appearance-intro"><p>See both sides before you choose. Each Mac download pairs the light and dark artwork in one file.</p><p class="appearance-format">Free HEIC download · Original desktop dimensions</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="appearance-downloads">
      {wallpaperDesigns.map(design => (
        <article class="appearance-design" aria-labelledby={`pairing-${design.slug}`}>
          <div class="appearance-previews">
            <figure><img src={previewHref(design.slug, 'light')} alt={`${design.name} light desktop artwork`} width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Light</figcaption></figure>
            <figure><img src={previewHref(design.slug, 'dark')} alt={`${design.name} dark desktop artwork`} width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Dark</figcaption></figure>
          </div>
          <div class="appearance-design-heading"><h3 id={`pairing-${design.slug}`}>{design.name}</h3><span class="appearance-collection">{design.collection} collection</span></div>
          <p class="appearance-tagline">{design.tagline}</p>
          <div class="appearance-design-actions">
            <ButtonLink variant="unstyled" class="port-button port-button-primary appearance-download" href={`/downloads/appearance/${design.slug}.heic`} ariaLabel={`Download pair — ${design.name} HEIC`} download><span>Download pair</span><Icon name="download" /></ButtonLink>
            <Link class="appearance-detail" href={wallpaperHref(design.slug)} aria-label={`Explore design — ${design.name}`}>Explore design <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="appearance-archive">Looking for an earlier design? Browse the <Link href="/gallery/archive/">Classic archive</Link>.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="iphone" class="site-shell port-section"><Eyebrow>On your iPhone</Eyebrow><h2>Two saved pairs. A daily rhythm.</h2><div class="port-columns"><ol class="port-steps"><li><h3>Save both wallpaper pairs</h3><p>Use the <Link href="/iphone/">iPhone setup pack</Link> to create a light pair and a dark pair in Settings → Wallpaper. Keep their clocks and widgets readable.</p></li><li><h3>Create a shortcut for each pair</h3><p>In Shortcuts, add Switch Between Wallpapers and select the saved light pair. Repeat for dark. Add Set Appearance to each if you also want the shortcut to set the matching system appearance.</p></li><li><h3>Schedule sunrise and sunset</h3><p>Create a Time of Day automation at Sunrise to run the light shortcut, and one at Sunset to run the dark shortcut, repeating daily. Enable immediate or unattended running where available, then test both shortcuts manually.</p></li></ol><aside class="port-card"><h3>A schedule you control</h3><p>Changing Dark Mode separately in Control Center does not trigger this schedule. Run the matching shortcut when you want to change both together. Auto icon appearance also leaves your saved wallpaper selection alone.</p><p>Alternatively, link each pair to a Focus you already use. Check its notification settings: Focus changes more than the wallpaper. Disable the automations when restoring your old setup.</p><div class="port-resources"><Link href="https://support.apple.com/guide/shortcuts/apd932ff833f/ios" newTab>Apple’s automation triggers</Link><Link href="https://support.apple.com/101583" newTab>Apple’s wallpaper shortcut actions</Link></div></aside></div></section>
  <section id="coverage" class="site-shell port-section port-columns"><div><Eyebrow>Keep it simple</Eyebrow><h2>Your artwork. Your choice.</h2></div><div><p>Mac downloads contain appearance metadata and two still images. iPhone uses your own saved wallpaper pairs; a Mac HEIC does not install a pair on iOS. No app, subscription, or configuration profile is required.</p><div class="port-related"><Link href="/gallery/">Explore all wallpaper formats</Link><Link href="/iphone/">Get the iPhone setup pack</Link></div></div></section>
</ProductLayout>
<style>
  .appearance-pair { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .appearance-pair img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--site-card-radius); border: 1px solid var(--site-line); }
  .appearance-pair > figcaption { margin-top: 0; }
  .appearance-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr; align-items: end; gap: var(--site-editorial-gap); margin-bottom: var(--site-heading-gap); }
  .appearance-heading h2 { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .appearance-heading h2 span { white-space: nowrap; }
  .appearance-intro { max-width: 42ch; }
  .appearance-intro p { margin: 0; }
  .appearance-intro .appearance-format { margin-top: 16px; font-size: .75rem; }
  .appearance-downloads { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--site-heading-gap) var(--site-grid-gap); }
  .appearance-design { min-width: 0; padding-bottom: 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--section-divider); }
  .appearance-previews { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .appearance-previews figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .appearance-previews img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border: 1px solid var(--site-line); border-radius: var(--site-control-radius); }
  .appearance-previews figcaption { margin-top: 10px; color: var(--site-ink-soft); font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .appearance-design-heading { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px 16px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .appearance-design-heading h3 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.2vw, 2rem); line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.055em; }
  .appearance-collection { color: var(--site-ink-soft); font-size: .6875rem; text-transform: capitalize; }
  .appearance-design .appearance-tagline { margin-block: 8px 20px; font-size: .8125rem; }
  .appearance-design-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px 24px; }
  .appearance-design-actions :global(a) { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: var(--site-control-min-height); font-size: .75rem; }
  .appearance-design-actions :global(.ui-icon) { width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .appearance-design-actions :global(.appearance-detail) { text-decoration: none; }
  .appearance-design-actions :global(.appearance-detail:hover) { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .appearance-design-actions :global(a:focus-visible) { outline: 2px solid var(--site-brand); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .port-section .appearance-archive { margin-block: 28px 0; font-size: .8125rem; }
  @media (max-width: 767px) { .appearance-heading, .appearance-downloads { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .appearance-heading { gap: 24px; } }
  @media (max-width: 380px) { .appearance-design-actions { gap: 8px 16px; } .appearance-design-actions :global(.appearance-download) { padding-inline: 16px; } }
</style>
